# Next.js app folders

Dashboard and landing share this `src/` layout. New files go in the matching folder.

| Folder | Holds |
| --- | --- |
| `app/` | App Router — pages, layouts, route handlers |
| `components/` | UI |
| `hooks/` | React hooks |
| `config/` | Env and app config |
| `lib/` | Wrappers around libraries (Drizzle, Better Auth, third-party SDKs) |
| `utils/` | Helper functions we wrote |
| `actions/` | Server Actions |
| `types/` | Shared TS types that are not a library's |

## lib vs utils

`lib/` is the seam onto a library. `utils/` is ours.

- `lib/db/index.ts` — the app's Drizzle connection (`export const db`)
- `lib/auth/` — Better Auth server (`index.ts`) and client (`client.ts`)
- `utils/auth/` — session lookup, Owner/Staff gates, role labels

shadcn CLI writes `cn` to `lib/utils.ts`. Leave that path so `shadcn add` keeps working.

```ts
// lib/db/index.ts
import { createDatabase } from "@dtm/database";
import { env } from "@/config/env";

export const db = createDatabase(env.DATABASE_URL);
```

```ts
// ✅
import { db } from "@/lib/db";
import { auth } from "@/lib/auth";
import { getSession } from "@/utils/auth/get-session";

// ❌ app connection re-exported as a factory; session helpers parked in lib/
import { createDatabase } from "@/lib/database";
import { getSession } from "@/lib/require-staff";
```
